# Blog Writing Rules for Medium Publishing

## Writing Style
- Write in a conversational, engaging tone
- Use clear, concise sentences
- Include personal anecdotes and examples
- Write for a general audience (avoid jargon without explanation)
- Aim for 800-2000 words per post

## Structure Guidelines
- Start with a compelling hook or question
- Use descriptive subheadings (H2, H3)
- Include bullet points and numbered lists for readability
- End with a clear call-to-action or thought-provoking conclusion
- Add relevant tags (up to 5) for Medium

## Content Requirements
- Include a meta description (150-160 characters)
- Add an engaging title (50-60 characters)
- Use relevant keywords naturally
- Include at least one image suggestion
- Add internal/external links where appropriate

## Medium-Specific Formatting
- Use # for main headings
- Use ## for subheadings
- Use ### for sub-subheadings
- Use **bold** for emphasis
- Use *italics* for subtle emphasis
- Use > for blockquotes
- Use - for bullet points
- Use 1. for numbered lists

## SEO Considerations
- Include target keywords in title and first paragraph
- Use descriptive alt text for images
- Create compelling meta descriptions
- Structure content with proper heading hierarchy
